  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Grain storage support for Ukrainian farms</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The impact of the project will be the expansion of storage capacity at a critical time of harvest for Ukrainian producers of grain and oil seeds. With the identification of local needs and assessment of options per oblast and by raion, FAO in coordination with the MAPF will provide alternative storage technologies such as polythene sleeves, loaders and unloaders as well as modular granariesin strategic 
areas.
The longer-term impact of the project will be ensuring the viability of grain and oil seed crop agriculture in Ukraine, sustaining global supplies and protecting the Ukrainian economy. This, in turn, will strengthen food security at the household and national levels in Ukraine, protect livelihoods and ensure other dependent countries retain access to adequate supplies of grain, at a manageable unit cost.</narrative>
  </description>
